# {{project_name}}

Generated by the `automation-generation` skill (binding `shaft-java-testng`) from the
approved test cases with `Needs Automation = TRUE`. See `../AutomationGeneration.md`
for the case mapping, locators and validation.

## Prerequisites

- JDK {{java_level}} (a JRE is not enough), Maven 3.6+, Google Chrome (Selenium Manager
  resolves the driver); network access to {{base_url}} and Maven Central
- SHAFT_ENGINE {{shaft_version}} — the newest release compiled for Java {{java_level}}

## Environment variables

| Name | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `{{username_env_var}}` | yes | Login user name — never stored in the project |
| `{{password_env_var}}` | yes | Login password — typed with `typeSecure`, masked in the report |
| `QA_BASE_URL` | no | Entry point (default `{{base_url}}`) |
| `QA_BROWSER` | no | `chromium`/`chrome` (default), `firefox`, `edge` |
| `QA_HEADLESS` | no | `true` (default) / `false` |
| `QA_TIMEOUT_MS` | no | Element / wait timeout (default {{default_timeout_ms}}) |
| `QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR` | no | Evidence root (default `{{default_artifacts_dir}}`) |
| `QA_RUN_ID` | no | Run identifier used in evidence paths |

## Run from the command line (Claude Code)

```
# set JAVA_HOME to a JDK {{java_level}} and the two credential variables, then:
mvn test
```

Windows profile path containing a space: SHAFT runs its Allure CLI from `user.home`
without quoting. Pass the 8.3 short form of the same folder:
`mvn test "-Dshaft.extraArgLine=-Duser.home=<short path>"`.

## Run from IntelliJ IDEA (Community)

Open `pom.xml` as a project (SDK: JDK {{java_level}}); Run > Edit Configurations >
**{{run_name}}** (TestNG suite, shared in `.run/`): fill the credential variables locally; run.

## Results

`<QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR>/<run-id>/{{binding_dir}}/<case-id>/`: `steps.log`, `final.png` or
`failure.png`. SHAFT: `allure-report/*_AllureReport.html`, `allure-results/`;
Surefire: `target/surefire-reports/`. SHAFT writes default property and listener files
into the project on each run (git-ignored). Retries are 0.
